            instructions: {
                en: "Show `name` and `dept_name` for all employees and all departments, matched or not.",
                id: "Tampilkan `name` dan `dept_name` untuk semua karyawan dan semua departemen, baik yang cocok maupun tidak."
            },
            seed_sql: mod5Seed,
            expected_query: "SELECT employees.name, departments.dept_name FROM employees FULL JOIN departments ON employees.department_id = departments.id;",
            starterQuery: "SELECT * FROM employees;",
            table_names: [
                "employees",
                "departments"
            ],
            engineOverrides: {
                mysql: {
                    title: {
                        en: "Cartesian Grid with CROSS JOIN (Var #5)",
                        id: "Perkalian Kartesian dengan CROSS JOIN (Latihan #5)"
                    },
                    conceptExplanation: {
                        en: "Conceptual Analogy: A CROSS JOIN produces a Cartesian product between two tables, pairing every row from the first table with every single row from the second table, like generating every possible combination of pizza crusts and topping selections.\n\nEngine Processing Behavior: The storage engine executes a nested loop join without join predicates or matching conditions, outputting N x M total rows (e.g. 8 employees x 4 departments = 32 rows). The engine allocates intermediate buffer memory to hold the multiplying combinatorial tuples before streaming to the client.\n\nBest Practices & Gotchas: PERFORMANCE WARNING: Never execute an unconstrained CROSS JOIN on large tables in production! A Cartesian product between two 100,000-row tables generates 10,000,000,000 rows, causing fatal memory exhaustion (OOM) and database server crashes. Only use CROSS JOIN for small fixed-matrix generation (such as calendar dates, grid coordinates, or matrix reporting).",
                        id: "Analogi Konseptual: CROSS JOIN menghasilkan perkalian Kartesian (Cartesian Product) antara dua tabel, memasangkan setiap satu baris dari tabel pertama dengan seluruh baris dari tabel kedua, persis seperti membuat matriks kombinasi antara jenis adonan pizza dan variasi topping.\n\nCara Kerja Database Engine: Database engine mengeksekusi nested loop join murni tanpa predikat kondisi pembanding (tanpa klausa ON), menghasilkan total N x M baris data (contohnya 8 karyawan x 4 departemen = 32 baris). Engine mengalokasikan memori buffer sementara untuk menampung pelipatgandaan kombinasi tuple ini sebelum di-stream ke result set client.\n\nBest Practices & Catatan Penting: PERINGATAN PERFORMA: Hindari penggunaan CROSS JOIN tanpa filter pada tabel berukuran besar di database production! Perkalian kartesian antara dua tabel berisi 100.000 baris akan memproduksi 10.000.000.000 baris data yang seketika memicu Out-of-Memory (OOM) dan menumbangkan server database. Gunakan CROSS JOIN hanya untuk kasus khusus pembuatan matriks kecil terukur (seperti matriks kalender tanggal, varian produk kecil, atau kombinasi grid analitik)."
                    },
                    syntaxPatterns: [
                        {
                            label: {
                                en: "Cartesian product via CROSS JOIN",
                                id: "Perkalian kartesian via CROSS JOIN"
                            },
                            code: "SELECT e.name, d.dept_name FROM employees e CROSS JOIN departments d ORDER BY e.name, d.dept_name;"
                        }
                    ],
                    instructions: {
                        en: "Generate every possible combination of employee `name` and department `dept_name`, sorted by `employees.name` and then `departments.dept_name`.",
                        id: "Tampilkan seluruh kombinasi yang mungkin antara nama karyawan (`name`) dan nama departemen (`dept_name`), diurutkan berdasarkan `employees.name` lalu `departments.dept_name`."
                    },
                    expected_query: "SELECT employees.name, departments.dept_name FROM employees CROSS JOIN departments ORDER BY employees.name, departments.dept_name;",
                    starterQuery: "SELECT * FROM employees;"
                }
            }
